Let me scroll and look more carefully. Actually maybe the badge only shows for tasks with a due time, not just date. Hmm.\n\nIn Tasks.org, list rows show due date badge on the right when the task has a due date. It typically displays like \"Nov 19\" in red if overdue, etc. Here I see nothing. Let me zoom the screenshot... I can't zoom, but the screenshot at 1080 wide: right side of rows is empty. So likely due date badge missing — but wait, the row's due_date View exists at x=1038. Hmm, maybe text is rendered but very light? No.\n\nActually maybe my view of the screenshot: the row \"Buy milk\" spans to x~1080. There's nothing at right. So the badge is empty. That seems like a bug: \"Date badges on task rows: the badge for each date field is now built independently of the others.\" Perhaps the badge for due date is broken because of the change.\n\nLet's observe more maybe scroll. Let me dismiss the banner first.\n\nActually, the elements list: TextView id=due_date exists, so there's a view but perhaps empty text. Interesting.\n\nLet me tap \"More options\" to check settings maybe. First dismiss banner.\n\nLet me plan carefully with steps and test each area.\n\nStep 1: Dismiss alarm banner.\nStep 2: Examine rows. Check due badges.\nStep 3: Open sort menu, test sorting/grouping.\nStep 4: Open Buy milk task editor, check date settings, time shortcuts in date picker.\nStep 5: Check settings date/time preferences.\nStep 6: Subtasks - expand/collapse, nesting indentation.\nStep 7: Repeating task Pay rent - edit, check repeat settings.\nStep 8: Rotation.\nStep 9: Add/modify? We can test by editing existing tasks maybe. Careful.\n\nLet me start."}
