{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa! Now with Read docs overdue (Nov 13), the header is \"Overdue\" and the due date badge appears: TextView \"Nov 13\" id=due_date at (981,429). So overdue tasks show a badge with date! Interesting. So the date badge DOES exist for overdue tasks. For future due dates, no badge? Hmm.\n\nWait, but maybe the badge is shown because \"Show full date\" is ON; for future dates, the badge should show \"Nov 19\" etc. But earlier with Show full date OFF, no badge. Now ON, overdue shows \"Nov 13\". Did I check other rows with Show full date ON? At the time (screenshot after toggling ON), all tasks future, no badges. So overdue shows badge but future doesn't? That seems odd.\n\nHmm wait, maybe badge depends on \"grouping\" header giving the date, so for date-grouped tasks the badge is redundant and hidden? In tasks.org, when grouped by due date, the due date badge is hidden? Hmm! That might be the actual behavior: when grouping by due date, each group header already shows the due date, so the row badge for due date is suppressed. But overdue group header doesn't show exact date, so the badge shows \"Nov 13\". Hmm, that's plausible stock behavior! Actually in tasks.org, I do recall that when grouped by due date, due dates may be hidden from rows since redundant... but then the \"date badge\" feature wouldn't generally show? Hmm.\n\nWait, but the row badge for start date should still show (start date differs from group's due date). We tested Buy milk with start date today + due Nov 19 while grouped by due date; no start badge appeared. Hmm, but maybe start badges are only shown when grouping isn't by due date? Unclear.\n\nLet me test: change grouping to \"None\" (no grouping) and see if badges appear for future tasks. That would reveal whether badges appear normally in ungrouped list. But the changed feature is about rows' date badge building independent of each other; maybe the bug is that when grouped by due date, due badge hidden (by design) but start badge should show... Hmm.\n\nLet me think about tasks.org's actual behavior (I can recall from using the app): In the task list with default settings (group by due date?), rows show date badges on the right. Hmm.\n\nActually, I think the app's default is grouping by \"None\" maybe, and sorting by due date. But here grouping is \"By due date\". With grouping by due date, the due date badges might be redundant. In tasks.org, I believe date badges still show. Hmm.\n\nLet me switch grouping to none to check.\n\nSort sheet: grouping \"By due date\" — tap element 2 to change grouping. Let's open sort menu."}
