d date normally.\n\nHmm, actually, maybe tasks.org supports \"relative start dates\" as a first-class feature: In Tasks.org, a task's \"start date\" can be set as \"1 day before due\" and this relation persists if due date changes. I don't think that exists; that's more like \"Google Tasks\"? Hmm. In Todoist, reminders relative to due date exist. In Tasks.org, no.\n\nGiven the editor displayed \"Day before due\" and after saving the list chip shows \"Wed\", the relation is not persisted as relative (chip shows absolute). Wait, unless the chip intentionally shows resolved relative. On reopening the editor, if it shows \"Wed\" then the label was just transient. Let me check: open Buy milk editor now. If start date row shows \"Wednesday, November 18\" (or \"Wednesday\"), then the \"Day before due\" was transient label; if it still shows \"Day before due\", it's persistent relative."}
