{"type": "thinking", "text": "The editor due row shows \"Saturday, November 21 at 9 AM\" (full date), not \"Saturday\". Hmm! So the editor date label for Nov 21 with Show full date OFF is FULL date. But earlier, the due date picker's current-date label for Nov 16 showed \"Monday\" (relative) and Nov 20 \"Friday\" (relative). Wait, the editor row for Nov 16 earlier (with Show full date ON) showed \"Monday, November 16\". With OFF, what does the editor show for Nov 16? We had Buy milk due Nov 19 and editor showed \"Thursday\" (short) with OFF. So editor short = weekday for +5. For +7 (Nov 21) editor shows full \"Saturday, November 21\". So the app's relative boundary is ≤6 days. The group header also full at +7. Consistent! So no inconsistency.\n\nSo boundary ≤6 seems the app-wide rule: editor, group header. What about badges? With OFF, badge for +5 \"Thu\", +10 \"Nov 24\". For +7 would likely be \"Nov 21\". The hidden \"Tmrw 9AM\" for tomorrow. Could test but likely consistent.\n\nThus grouping boundaries seem correct (≤6 relative, ≥7 full). So no bug.\n\nUgh. Okay, where are the bugs? Let me look at the actual precondition data and compare with what's displayed:\n- Buy milk due in 5 days: shown group \"Due Thursday\" — correct.\n- Pack for trip due in 10 days: \"Due Tuesday, November 24\" — correct.\n- Pay rent due in 20 days: \"Due Friday, December 4\" — correct.\n- Read docs no due: \"No due date\" — correct.\n- Notes: \"2 litres\" displayed; link displayed.\n- Subtask count \"2\"; nested indentation.\n- Repeat icon for Pay rent.\n\nMaybe the bug is that Buy milk's due date is 5 days from *today*, but the group header \"Due Thursday\" is correct. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the seeded bugs are in the *editor date settings*—e.g., the due date row when tapped shows time shortcuts from preferences, but maybe the *date shortcuts* (\"Today/Tomorrow/Next Sat\") are wrong in some boundary. We tested Today→today, Tomorrow→tomorrow, Next Sat→Nov 21. Correct.\n\nHmm, what about \"No date\" clearing both date and time? We did that; it cleared. Good.\n\nWhat about \"No time\" clearing time while keeping date? Let's test: set due date with 9AM, then tap a date/time... Actually \"No time\" should clear time. We can test on Read docs: currently due Nov 21 9AM. Open picker, tap \"No time\", OK → due row should show \"Saturday, November 21\" (no time). Then Save. Then revert.\n\nNot likely bug.\n\nMaybe I should check the \"Next Sat\" shortcut boundary when today is not Saturday... not possible.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider the time shortcuts preference test. The picker labels times using the *display* of preferences. We changed Morning to 7 AM and it showed 7 AM. But maybe the *bug* is that changing preferences doesn't update an already-open picker? Not important. So feature works.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug in time shortcuts: after changing Morning to 7 AM, the picker showed 7 AM, but did the *second* slot show 1 PM (Afternoon), third 5 PM, fourth 8 PM. Yes. So all good.\n\nHold on—maybe the bug is in the *ordering*: the date picker lists time shortcuts as Morning, Afternoon, Evening, Night in the settings, but the picker order is 9 AM, 1 PM, 5 PM, 8 PM. That matches. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug involves seconds/rounding when preference has minutes: e.g., set Morning to 9:30; picker shows \"9:30 AM\"; tapping it sets 9:30. We could test but likely fine.\n\nWhat if the preferences have duplicate times? irrelevant.\n\nLet me look at the task list options for row display: \"Show full task title\" off, row spacing 16, font 16, \"Show description\" on, \"Show full description\" off, \"Show links\" off. In the row, the description \"See https://example.com/guide\" is displayed (because description) — the link is shown as part of description (not linkified). \"Show links\" off means links aren't tappable. Fine.\n\nWait: The precondition says Read docs' notes contain the link. The row shows \"See https://example.com/guide\" — but where did \"See \" come from? Maybe the note is literally \"See https://example.com/guide\". Fine.\n\nHmm, maybe the bug is that the description shows the link but \"Show links\" is off — irrelevant.\n\nLet me check the task editor for Read docs: notes field \"See https://example.com/guide\". Good.\n\nMaybe test adding a new task? The task list \"how each row is shown\" might have missing due badge when grouped by due date (by design). Hmm.\n\nLet me think about the possibility that the seeded bug is the *missing due date badge in grouped view* after all. In stock Tasks.org, does the due date badge show in grouped-by-due-date view? Let me think of the actual app: When grouping by due date, each group header shows \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\", \"Nov 21\" etc. Rows under them do NOT show a due date badge on the right (since redundant) — I'm fairly confident this is stock. Actually hmm, I've used Tasks.org; default grouping is \"By due date\"? I remember rows with dates on the right even when grouped. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the app's own behavior with \"By start date\" grouping: When grouping by start date, do due badges show? Probably yes (since due date isn't the grouping header). That would confirm the logic \"hide badge for the field being grouped by\". Let me test: change grouping to \"By start date\" and see: Buy milk (no start) in \"No start date\" group, due badges shown? Read docs has start tomorrow → group \"Tomorrow\"? with due badge? If badges appear, then the app hides due badges only when grouped by due date, consistent design. That's likely intended. Fine.\n\nOK, maybe there are no bugs in the four changed areas, but there might be a bug in another part. Let me sweep systematically:\n\nTask list:\n- Sorting menu & grouping menu: tested partially. Maybe test \"By priority\" grouping to see if priorities show correctly? All tasks have no priority (except maybe none). Hmm, not meaningful.\n- Search: test search finds tasks. Search \"milk\" → Buy milk. Could reveal a bug? Unlikely but let's test quickly.\n- Completion: completing a task creates bug? Not changed. Testing completion modifies data; can undo. Subtasks completing maybe.\n- Row display: due badges, start chips, subtask count, repeat icon, notes.\n\nTask editor:\n- Title editing, notes editing (persistence). We haven't saved any text edits; we can test editing notes then reverting. Risk manageable. E.g., edit Read docs notes to \"test\", save, reopen, revert. This tests persistence. Probably fine.\n- Priority radio: click blue radio on Read docs, save, verify, revert. Probably fine.\n- Tags/lists.\n- Date settings: tested.\n- Repeating: verify Pay rent repeats monthly in editor. Maybe test completion behavior? Risky.\n- Subtasks: add/remove tested.\n\nHmm, maybe the bug is in the repeating task: Pay rent \"Repeats monthly\" but maybe the repetition is actually e.g. \"Repeats every 1 month from due date\" okay. Let me open the repeat picker to see options. Earlier tapping the repeat row toggled the \"from\" chip. There might be a separate way to edit the repeat rule: In tasks.org, tapping the repeat row opens a repeat picker sheet with options (None, Daily, Weekly, Monthly, Yearly, Custom). Let me try tapping the repeat row's left part (the \"Repeats monthly\" label area) — maybe opens the repeat selection dialog. Earlier tapping element 5 center toggled the from chip; perhaps the label itself is a button. Elements: [5] View contains \"Repeats monthly\" | \"Repeats from\" | \"due date\" clickable @(540,856); [6] View contains \"due date\" clickable @(589,907). It seems the whole row is clickable to toggle? Hmm. Maybe tapping element 5 toggled because it hit the chip? The row includes the chip; a tap at center (540,856) is above the chip (y=907)? Actually row [5] center y=856, chip at y=907. Tap at (540,856) shouldn't hit the chip. Yet it toggled \"due date\"→\"completion date\". So tapping the row toggles the repeat-from mode. Maybe repeated taps cycle? Hmm. Then where do you choose the repeat frequency (monthly)? Maybe tapping the row opens a new screen? The observe after tap showed the same editor with from=completion date. So tapping the row toggles `from due date` vs `from completion date` (a clickable label near repeat). To edit frequency, maybe there's a separate control. The row text \"Repeats monthly\" + \"Repeats from\" + \"due date\" suggests row layout:", "truncated": true}
