{"type": "thinking", "text": "Grouping restored. Now, Read docs has due Tomorrow 9AM + start \"Due date\" (relative, resolves to Nov 15). Need to restore to no start and no due date. Do that at the end. But before that, maybe use this state for more tests.\n\nWait! I notice something: In the grouped-by-due-date view, Read docs row (due tomorrow) shows a due badge \"9 AM\" at right. Earlier, tasks in \"Due Thursday\" group showed no due badge (empty TextView). But for Read docs (due tomorrow 9AM), the badge shows \"9 AM\". Interesting: the due badge is not hidden when the due date has a *time*? It shows only the time \"9 AM\", while the group header shows \"Due tomorrow\". So the app hides the date part but shows the time. That's sensible: badge shows time when grouped by due date. So the due badge always exists but its text for grouped-by-due-date is only the time (if any). Good—this changes my understanding: the due badge is hidden when grouped by due date except time. Consistent.\n\nSo no bug.\n\nHmm OK. Let me think about the \"date badges independently\" change again: It might refer to exactly this: when grouping by due date, the badge for the due date shows only the time; the badge for the start date shows the date. Previously a single badge was built from one date field for both, causing e.g. start chip to show the due date's time or vice versa. The change fixed that. The test: task with start date and due time, grouped by due date, should show start chip date AND due badge time independently. Our Read docs has start \"Due date\" (hidden? in grouped view, start chip should show) and due time 9AM. In the current grouped view, does Read docs row show a start chip? Elements: [2] header \"Due tomorrow\", [3] rowBody contains \"Read docs\" | description — no start chip! Hmm! Read docs has a start date (start = due date = Nov 15). In the due-date-grouped view, the start chip should be shown (since not grouped by start date). But the rowBody doesn't contain any start