{"type": "thinking", "text": "Note the editor shows due \"Tuesday\" — but Nov 10, 2026 is a Tuesday? Yes. But wait, for a past date, the editor shows \"Tuesday\" (weekday only) — maybe should show \"Tuesday, November 10\"? Hmm, with Show full date OFF, relative labels for a date 4 days ago? The picker earlier showed Nov 10 as \"November 10\" (top row after selecting). Interesting! The start picker earlier showed \"November 21\" for +7; for -4 (Nov 10) the due picker top row showed \"November 10\". But the editor due row shows \"Tuesday\". Hmm! So the editor date label formats past dates as weekday (Tuesday) while the picker's current-date label formats as \"November 10\". Inconsistent formats again, but maybe the editor uses a different formatter (relative short) intentionally: for dates within ±6 days, weekday; beyond, full date. Nov 10 is -4 days → weekday \"Tuesday\". That seems consistent with a ±6 window. The picker's current label \"November 10\" maybe uses a different format including month for past? Hmm.\n\nWait, that could be the bug! The due date picker's first row for a selected date shows \"November 10\" (month+day) for Nov 10 (-4 days), while the editor shows \"Tuesday\". Inconsistent. But which is correct? Eh, formatters differ; not necessarily a bug.\n\nAnyway, Save and observe groups with two overdue tasks."}
