{"type": "thinking", "text": "Base state restored (grouping by due date, sorting ascending). \n\nNow, let me reconsider potential bug in date badges: Maybe the bug is that when grouping by due date, the due date badge for tasks with a *time* shows the time only (e.g., \"9 AM\") — but the start chip might also show only time or something. Hmm.\n\nWait, I realize I haven't checked the **start date badge when start date has a time**. In tasks.org, the start date chip shows date and maybe time. If start date has a time, the chip should show the time. The changed note \"badge for each date field built independently\" might have a bug where the time is taken from the wrong field. Test: set Buy milk start date Nov 16 9 AM (or start today with time), due Nov 19 (no time). Then see the start chip: does it show \"Mon\" (date) or \"9 AM\" (time)? The chip should probably show \"Mon 9 AM\" or just \"Mon\"? Hmm. In the due badge, when due date has time (ungrouped), it shows \"Tmrw 9 AM\". So start chip with time probably shows \"Mon 9 AM\". If it shows only \"9 AM\" or wrong time, maybe bug. Hmm.\n\nGiven the changed note explicitly says \"badge for each date field is now built independently of the others\", I'd guess the seeded bug is that the start-date badge (chip) shows the *due date* (or due time), or the due-date badge shows the start date. Our tests showed correct values for date parts though. Maybe with times there's a cross-contamination. Let's test: Buy milk: start date = Nov 16 (Mon) with start time 9 AM; due date Nov 19 with no time. Then ungrouped view: start chip should show \"Mon 9 AM\"? and due badge \"Thu\". Then change start time to 5 PM and see chip update \"Mon 5 PM\" while due badge unchanged \"Thu\". This directly tests independence of time components.\n\nHmm, this is getting elaborate. But let's do it, because it's the changed feature most likely to harbor the bug.\n\nPlan:\n1. Open Buy milk.\n2. Set start date Nov 16 (calendar) + start time 9 AM? The start picker has time shortcuts 9 AM,1PM,5PM,8PM. Tap Nov 16 then 9 AM then OK. (Note the start date picker's time shortcuts: tapping time may adjust date if in the past—Nov 16 future so fine.)\n3. Set due time? Due Nov 19 no time. We want due unchanged. Actually to test \"start chip time vs due badge\", due has no time → due badge \"Thu\". Start chip \"Mon 9 AM\".\n4. Save; switch grouping None; observe chip & badge.\n5. Reopen Buy milk; change start time to 5 PM; save; observe chip \"Mon 5 PM\", due badge \"Thu\" unchanged.\n6. Remove start date; restore grouping; done.\n\nLet's go. Open Buy milk (row 3)."}
